      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Belgian administration resisted change because their entire economic and social structure was built upon the systematic extraction of Congolese resources and labor. They clung to paternalistic justifications, claiming they were \"civilizing\" the population, which was a thinly veiled excuse to maintain absolute control and profit. Nationalist movements, meanwhile, steadily built momentum by organizing resistance against these exploitative policies year after year. This resistance was a direct rejection of the colonial premise that the Congolese were incapable of governing themselves.",
      "source": "target",
